Q: How to add a gradient to a Button in Flutter? A: <p>For anyone that does not want to wrap the button inside another <code>Widget</code>, please use</p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>ElevatedButton.styleFrom({
  backgroundBuilder: (context, states, child) {
    final ThemeData(:colorScheme) = Theme.of(context);
    final isDisabled = states.contains(WidgetState.disabled);

    return DecoratedBox(
      decoration: BoxDecoration(
        gradient: isDisabled ? null : LinearGradient(colors: [...])
        ...
      ),
      ...
      child: child,
    );
  },
})
</code></pre>
<p>In this way, the gradient will be correctly rendered behind the ripple and before the background color. And you still get all the benefits of using a framework button widget.</p>
<p>Same thing applies to <code>FilledButton</code>, <code>IconButton</code> and so on, as long as the button accepts a
<code>style</code>.</p>

